# init(8)

## NAME

init - the first process

## SYNOPSIS

    /sbin/init

## DESCRIPTION

init is started first when the computer boots (pid 1). It reads `/etc/inittab`, runs the `run` entries one by one, starts the `daemon` and `respawn` entries, and then starts the console shell in the foreground. A shell or `respawn` program that ends is started again.

Without `/etc/inittab`, init starts `/bin/sh` only.

## FILES

- `/etc/inittab`: what to start at boot

## SEE ALSO

inittab(5), sh(1)
